Local Audio Zones

This community app is based on Music Assistant Local Audio and its native
Sendspin player update in pull request 34:
https://github.com/music-assistant/local-audio-addon
https://github.com/music-assistant/local-audio-addon/pull/34

The packaging and startup code have been modified to provide independent room
players, native room configuration, validated channel routing, durable route
ownership, and separate supervision and saved state. The original Apache-2.0
license is retained in LICENSE.

The image builds sendspin-cpp-cli v0.2.0, commit
e980128a9c37229cbc28c764e9f2fd65d1c5edb6, and sendspin-cpp v0.8.0, commit
9331ace6428979982c934384702d289958ca125e.
Copyright 2026 sendspin-cpp-cli Contributors.
Copyright 2026 Kevin Ahrendt (sendspin-cpp).
Both projects use the Apache License, Version 2.0. Local patches pin named
PulseAudio outputs using PA_STREAM_DONT_MOVE and keep bounded audio-device
recovery available through long and repeated disconnections.
https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-cpp-cli
https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-cpp

The native player also includes ArduinoJson v7.4.1 (MIT), IXWebSocket v11.4.5
(BSD-3-Clause with separately licensed embedded code), micro-flac v0.1.1,
micro-opus v0.3.5 and micro-ogg-demuxer v1.2.0 (Apache-2.0), and Opus v1.6.1
(BSD licenses and upstream patent-license references). micro-opus applies its
own patches to the Opus source. Their full license texts, source notices and
verified commits are retained in licenses/. These dependencies retain their
own licenses; the app's Apache-2.0 license does not replace them.

The icon adapts the HASSConnect house artwork with room speaker symbols.
HASSConnect is Copyright (c) 2026 alphasixtyfive, under the MIT license retained
in HASSCONNECT-LICENSE. https://github.com/alphasixtyfive/HASSConnect

Local Audio Zones is independently maintained. Home Assistant and Music
Assistant names identify compatibility and upstream origin, not endorsement.

The USB relay controller is an independent implementation. Its LCUS protocol
and shared-amplifier behaviour were checked against Multi-Room Audio's .NET
implementation (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Squeezelite Multi-Room Docker Controller).
No .NET implementation code is included.
